{"chunk_id": "c9bac7574817", "text": "In this section the Pandavas dwell in the sacred hermitage of Nara and Narayana near the Bhagirathi, enjoying a serene landscape of flowering woods, lakes, and mountains while awaiting Arjuna\u2019s return from heaven. The calm is broken when a celestial thousand\u2011petaled lotus is blown to them by the wind. Enchanted by its fragrance, Draupadi asks Bhima to gather more of these rare flowers for their hermitage. Eager to please her, Bhima sets off alone toward the Gandhamadana mountain, striding through forests with overwhelming strength that terrifies beasts and shakes the wilderness. His journey becomes both a display of heroic power and inner reflection on his brothers and their exile. At last his thunderous approach awakens Hanuman, the mighty monkey hero\u2014Bhima\u2019s divine brother\u2014who blocks the path and begins to challenge and instruct him, setting the stage for a significant encounter about strength and humility.\nDraupadi asks Bhima to fetch celestial lotuses; he storms through Gandhamadana, terrifying beasts, until Hanuman blocks his path and questions his conduct.\nThemes: heroic quest, nature's grandeur, devotion to Draupadi, strength and pride, divine encounter", "vector": [0.004447559826076031, -0.02952703833580017, -0.02166285365819931, 0.004037829115986824, -0.006172393448650837, 0.049379147589206696, -0.013098162598907948, -0.00648629991337657, -0.020698003470897675, -0.02254839986562729, -0.00492337578907609, 0.001613314263522625, 0.029421301558613777, 0.0004530992591753602, 0.015226118266582489, 0.014367005787789822, 0.04337857663631439, -0.009859968908131123, 0.02053939923644066, -0.01719546876847744, -0.0074874963611364365, -0.010507607832551003, 0.00010439456673339009, 0.024530967697501183, -0.018689002841711044, 0.01531863771378994, 0.027174390852451324, -0.02849610336124897, 0.0026285541243851185, -0.005914659705013037, -0.01817353442311287, -0.0057957055978477, 0.001417535706423223, -0.00016